            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="d63-04" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve15p1/d63-04"/>

                <head>65. Memorandum From the Military Assistant to the Secretary of Defense
                        (Wickham) to the
                    Assistant Secretary of Defense for International Security Affairs (Hill), Washington, October 17,
                        1973.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d65-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d65-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1973-10-17"
                        >October 17, 1973</date>.</dateline>
                <pb facs="d65-01" n="1" xml:id="d65-01"/>
                <p>OFFICE OF THE SECRETARY OF DEFENSE</p>
                <p>WASHINGTON, D. C. 20301</p>
                <p>17 October 1973</p>
                <p>MEMORANDUM FOR: Assistant Secretary of Defense (ISA)</p>
                <p>SUBJECT: DOD Actions Underway with Yugoslavia</p>
                <p>The Secretary notes the attached memorandum.</p>
                <p>Until such time that a determination is made that the Yugoslavia Government takes
                    actions which are compatible with U.S. national security interests, the
                    Secretary directs that all DOD actions for
                    closer cooperation with Yugoslavia be suspended.</p>
                <p>
                    John A. Wickham, Jr. Major General,
                        USA Military Assistant</p>
                <p>Attachment</p>
                <p>X-4372</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d65-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d65-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Washington National Records Center, RG 330, Records of the Secretary of
                    Defense, OSD Files: FRC 330-78-001, Yugoslavia.
                    Confidential. The attached memorandum was not found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d65-f2" n="2" xml:id="d65-f2-content">
                <p>Secretary of Defense Schlesinger suspended the Department of Defense&amp;apos;s
                    activities to facilitate greater U.S.-Yugoslavian military cooperation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
